    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d265-a2">

                <pb facs="1317" n="1159" sameAs="frus:frus1906p2/pg1159"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Minister Gummeré to the Minister for Foreign
                        Affairs</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Tangier</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1906-04-19"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">April 19, 1906</hi>.</date></dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 32.]</seg></opener>
                <p>(After compliments:) I have the honor to acknowledge your excellency’s letter of
                    the 14th instant, informing me that a steamer belonging to Isaac Pinto, a
                    Spanish protégé of Tetuan, has landed a quantity of cartridges on the Riff
                    coast, and that when engaged in so doing he flies the American flag.</p>
                <p>In reply I have to inform your excellency that the boat in question, I have
                    reason to believe, belongs to an American citizen of Tangier, one Leon Osiel,
                    and, being duly registered, has the right to fly the American flag. This,
                    however, is no license for the carrying on of illegitimate business, and I need
                    not assure your excellency that nothing of the kind will be tolerated by this
                    legation. If any boat flying the American flag is proved to be engaged in any
                    illegitimate business, upon such proof being furnished to me, there will be no
                    hindrance interposed by this legation to the enforcement of the penalties of the
                    law.</p>
                <p>In peace,</p>
                <closer>(Signed) <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">S. R.
                    Gummeré.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
